Z||000000||elfiero||10-23-2000||02:50 PM||||Have any of you guys used those white gage<BR>overlays on the later GT clusters?Is it harder to see at night? any other comments<BR>about them?||||reg||5
Z||000001||BAM-BAM||10-23-2000||03:13 PM||||Elfiero, It would be harder to see at night on the 120MPH cluster because they are backlit. In the earlier 85MPH version they used offset lighting and it doesn't pose that problem. There are some for sale on E-Bay right now as we type. The guy even explains that. Some one here posted a couple of days ago about this. He said they look great in the daylight, but hard to seee at night. Try this  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/anniversarygt350/wfg.htm</A>  <BR> <P>  Later, BAM OUT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH<p>[This message has been edited by BAM-BAM (edited 10-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||10-23-2000||03:56 PM||||I used them on my "reflector-style" gauges:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/001925.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/001925.html</A> <P>I like the effect.  Only complaint I have is that, after only 6 months, they're beginning to peel.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||10-23-2000||05:29 PM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR>[B]I used them on my "reflector-style" gauges:<BR>i used the black faces from FieroStore on my 86. speedo goes to 200mph, tach 8,000 rpm. There backlit (thru the nmbrs from inside) I used laquer thinner to wipe all the face off of them first, makes dial all white. then put them on, works just like OEM at nite.||||reg||1
